'''Massive Medal Pusher''' (クソでっけぇプッシャーゲーム) is a cross-platform [[:Category:Game worlds|game world]] created by {{VRC link|https://vrchat.com/home/user/usr_194e211a-a2d2-4c01-a60d-230c6d05af75|りくち_}}. It left [[Special:MyLanguage/Community Labs|Community Labs]] on {{Date|April 12, 2025}}.<ref>[https://vrchat.com/home/world/wrld_1af53798-92a3-4c3f-99ae-a7c42ec6084d Massive Medal Pusher] on ''vrchat.com''.</ref> Players insert medals into a [[Wikipedia:Coin pusher|coin pusher]], drop them for a saved total, and spend that total on perks, skills, and totems.

== Layout ==

The world is a set of wooden rooms around a large pusher table. A golden dispenser box floats in the play area. Picking it up (or pressing 2 on desktop) inserts medals; the medals drop from a tower at the back of the table. A payout rail sits on the right. Balls come from a red rail in front of the table.

A roulette wheel sits above the pusher. A Sherbi Chance board sits with the physical lottery machine. Paletta and Ferretta lottery machines stand to the right of the pusher. Roomkeeper Sherbi figures spawn around the rooms.

The second floor holds a shrine with altars for totems, an in-world guide (SherPedia), achievement and statistics boards, and avatar pedestals. Cloud save and global leaderboards are on wall panels.

A keypad labels a management room. The in-world text tells players not to enter; doing so destroys save data.

The world is graphically heavy, so enabling avatar culling is recommended; mobile headsets drain battery quickly.<ref name="cwiki-home">[https://wikiwiki.jp/vr_bigpusher/ クソでっけぇプッシャーゲーム（でかプ） Wiki] (in Japanese). Retrieved {{Date|September 3, 2026}}.</ref>

== Gameplay ==

Inserted medals pile on the moving pusher shelf. Drops from the front pay the saved total. The payout counter, filled by roulette wins and ball drops, shoots extra medals from the right rail. Higher counters pay faster. When the counter is very large, compressed medals and golden medals replace ordinary payouts.

Manual insertion speeds up while the trigger is held. That extra speed lasts a short time on auto-insert after the player stops. Manual insertion also adds five times as much to the Sherbi jackpot progressive counter as auto-insert. Some perks that spawn SP medals or balls during insertion apply only to manual insertion unless a totem extends them.

Progress is stored with [[Special:MyLanguage/Persistence|Persistence]]. A cloud-save panel can back up that data and feeds the global leaderboard.

