=== Roulette ===

Each dropped Roulette Medal spins the wheel once. 5–100 WIN adds that many payout counts. BALL spawns a Sherbi Ball. LOSE pays nothing.

Fever spends one stored Fever spin per roulette. During Fever there is no LOSE, the minimum WIN is 10, the maximum WIN is 500, and high WIN and BALL are more common.

Landing 70 WIN or more lights one bonus-step lamp. Seven lamps fire one of: +100 payout, one 10-chain Lottery Ball, +15 Fever, or three random balls.

=== Sherbi Chance ===

Sherbi Chance unlocks at 1,000 total. A Lottery Ball that finishes the physical lottery moves Sherbi 1–8 squares.

* Blue or yellow: payout by the square
* Green: payout in green medals or higher (5×)
* BALL: that many Sherbi Balls
* JACKPOT: Sherbi Jackpot

Multipliers rise with laps that skip JACKPOT and with Lottery Ball chains. Extra balls from a multiplier do not keep the chain.

The Sherbi progressive counter in the center of the board is the jackpot payout. It is shared in the instance. It rises from medal drops, Navy balls, Sherbi Chance rewards, and Roomkeeper Sherbi, and falls when anyone in the instance hits jackpot. The drop has a 3-second cooldown per player and is smaller when more players are present. A local hard cap depends on progress.

Sherbi Jackpot pays the progressive counter times the Sherbi Chance multipliers, launches medals from above, and launches balls from the count. Ordinary payout during the jackpot is added to the jackpot counter.

ULTIMATE MODE can start from a Roomkeeper Sherbi or, rarely, from roulette. Every square becomes a red 100 WIN. Each advance raises the Sherbi Chance multiplier, then that square becomes END. Landing on END ends the mode. Yellow or JACKPOT clears END squares back to red.

=== Paletta Chance ===

Paletta unlocks at 1,000,000 total. A Paletta Ball appears after enough insertions, or on a very rare insertion roll. Dropping it starts the disk lottery on the right.

* Number: payout
* BALL: many Sherbi Balls
* NEXT: a higher-multiplier Paletta stage
* JACKPOT: Paletta Jackpot

The Paletta progressive counter is local and stored in temporary save data, one value per jackpot tier. It rises from non-JACKPOT pockets, rare medals and balls, Lavender balls, and Roomkeepers. Winning a Paletta Jackpot cuts that tier and lower tiers.

Paletta Jackpot pays the stored counter, launches medals from above, and launches balls (Special or better; every 10th ball is Rare or better). Payout during this jackpot is multiplied by 10 before it is added to the jackpot counter.

A Golden Paletta Ball doubles the lottery reward. Meadow balls add Golden Power, which raises the Paletta multiplier and Golden Paletta chance and decays after each Paletta lottery.

=== Ferretta Chance ===

Ferretta unlocks at 10,000,000 total. Every three Paletta Balls spawn one Ferretta Ball. The disk lottery marks numbers on a bingo card. Completing a line pays Ferretta Jackpot. Several lines at once raise the jackpot tier, up to five. Those numbers then deactivate.

The card starts with at least ten active squares and at least one square that can complete a line. If not, random numbers activate until both are true.

The Ferretta progressive counter is local on the bingo card. It rises from non-jackpot pockets (more with a Ferretta item), Lavender balls, and Roomkeepers, and drops on a Ferretta Jackpot. Golden Power also multiplies Ferretta Jackpot and is spent only on a win.

Ferretta items come from item pockets and from Black Boxes. Common, rare, and legendary items can open extra bingo hits.

=== Roomkeeper Sherbi ===

Roomkeeper Sherbi unlocks at 100 total. Figures spawn over time. Interacting pays a random reward. Spawn rate is higher when none are in the room and falls off after four. Rainbow Roomkeepers are stronger and rarer.

Non-rainbow Roomkeepers have a small chance to start ULTIMATE MODE instead of the usual reward. That chance rises with skill use, Roomkeeper interacts, and a weak previous ULTIMATE MODE, then resets when ULTIMATE MODE occurs.

=== Skills ===

SP medals pay skill points. Points also come from some balls, manual insertion, and Roomkeeper interacts. The skill shop spends them. Each skill also gives a smaller effect to other players in the instance. Holding a shop button repeats the skill. Skill points save with the rest of progress.

Visible skills include 50 Win, Special Ball, Fever Roulette, 20 Fever, and Rainbow Ball. Rainbow Ball costs 50 skill points and also spawns three extra balls; players who only receive the skill get ten random balls instead. A third skill slot unlocks at 2,000,000 total.

A credit shop sells timed auto-insert and faster roulette. Auto-insert does not trigger some perks that require manual insertion. Manual insertion while auto-insert is running pauses that timer.

A local setting can refuse other players' skills. Another local setting reduces 20× skill receive when an instance is heavy.

=== Tasks ===

Tasks unlock at 5,000 total. Repeatable tasks pay skill points when the objective is met. Daily tasks are three objectives that reset at {{Time|00:00}} UTC. Claiming all three daily tasks pays one Black Box. Completing any task also has a low chance of a Black Box: 3% plus the skill-point reward divided by 1,000. A Black Box also spawns one random gem Sherbi Ball.

=== Perks ===

The perk shop unlocks at 10,000 total. Each perk has levels 0–10. A respec refunds the spent total. Individual perks also have their own unlock conditions (insertions, roulette wins, jackpots, and similar).

