Navy and Lavender totem bonuses are instance-wide and shown on shrine counters. The shrine sign renames itself after the placed totems; with no totem placed it reads "Void Shrine" (虚無神社).<ref name="cwiki-totem" />

=== Achievements and leaderboards ===

An achievement board lists bronze, silver, gold, and platinum entries. Overhead nameplates can show achievement count. Cloud save feeds a global ranking of total earned and related stats. Instance ranking panels show Paletta and Ferretta jackpot records.

=== Strategy ===

Cream and Cyan are generally considered the strongest totems: Cream keeps a permanent multiplier on Sherbi Chance, and Cyan doubles its lottery attempts. Red, Green, Lime, and Mint (paired with Cyan) also rate highly. Orange, Navy, Meadow, Lavender, and Yellow are seen as weak, useful mainly for chasing ranking records rather than raw earnings.<ref name="cwiki-totem" />

A common five-altar loadout is Green, Red, Cream, Mint, and Cyan, swapping Green out when too many balls slow the instance down. Past that fixed set, players match totem placement, perk levels, and skill timing to the daily Sherbi, a featured ball color that changes each day.<ref name="cwiki-totem" /><ref name="cwiki-guide">[https://wikiwiki.jp/vr_bigpusher/%E5%88%9D%E5%BF%83%E8%80%85%E3%82%AC%E3%82%A4%E3%83%89 初心者ガイド] (in Japanese). クソでっけぇプッシャーゲーム Wiki. Retrieved {{Date|September 3, 2026}}.</ref>

New players usually level Faster Insertion and Skill Receiver first, summon the Lime totem before buying a third altar, and take Cream as the first 10-billion-medal summon.<ref name="cwiki-guide" />

Skills buff every other player in the instance, so populated instances are generally considered to progress much faster than playing alone.<ref name="cwiki-guide" /><ref>[https://vrc-world-guide.hatenablog.com/entry/koryaku-pusher 【VRChatワールド攻略】Massive Medal Pusherで億万長者になる3つのコツ] (in Japanese). oka-vrc旅行記, {{Date|October 19, 2025}}.</ref> During a Paletta Jackpot every payout is multiplied by 10, so raising the Sherbi jackpot progressive counter and landing Sherbi Jackpots inside that window is a favorite way to multiply earnings.<ref name="cwiki-guide" />

== Characters ==

'''Sherbi''' is a snow weasel used on medals, balls, Roomkeepers, and the Sherbi Chance board. The design uses a [https://booth.pm/en/items/3284766 KIGURUMI MARMOT] Booth asset.

'''Paletta''' is a ferret used on Paletta Balls and the Paletta lottery.

'''Ferretta''' is a ferret used on Ferretta Balls and the bingo lottery. Paletta and Ferretta use a [https://booth.pm/en/items/4944751 Nebula plant] Booth ferret asset.

